1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,342
If you hear your family calling your name
from the

2
00:00:03,362 --> 00:00:06,668
dark pine woods tonight, do not step
outside.

3
00:00:06,688 --> 00:00:12,643
A skinwalker only needs to hear a human
voice once to steal it forever.

4
00:00:12,663 --> 00:00:16,919
It stands nine feet tall at the edge of
the clearing,

5
00:00:16,939 --> 00:00:20,689
hiding its skeletal frame behind the
trees.

6
00:00:20,709 --> 00:00:23,847
But the voice coming from its throat
sounds

7
00:00:23,867 --> 00:00:27,234
identical to your mother or your sister.

8
00:00:27,254 --> 00:00:32,103
And it knows the exact trick that will
make you unlock the front door.

9
00:00:32,123 --> 00:00:33,896
Let us go back to the beginning.

10
00:00:34,496 --> 00:00:41,157
It was two fifteen in the morning when the
call began outside my forest cabin.

11
00:00:41,177 --> 00:00:44,573
I was sitting at my wooden desk when a
familiar

12
00:00:44,593 --> 00:00:47,784
voice floated through the open window.

13
00:00:47,804 --> 00:00:49,545
It was my sister Mira.

14
00:00:49,565 --> 00:00:54,078
She sounded desperate, pleading from the
edge of the fence,

15
00:00:54,098 --> 00:00:58,677
saying she had dropped her car keys in the
tall grass.

16
00:00:58,697 --> 00:01:04,575
My hand was on the brass deadbolt before
my brain caught up with the silence.

17
00:01:04,595 --> 00:01:07,531
Mira lived two hours away in the city.

18
00:01:07,551 --> 00:01:10,220
Her car was not in the driveway.

19
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:13,449
And she had not visited this cabin in
three months.

20
00:01:14,049 --> 00:01:18,400
I crept to the porch window and looked out
across the lawn.

21
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:22,197
At first, you think it must be a trick of
your mind.

22
00:01:22,217 --> 00:01:29,408
A normal throat cannot reproduce a human
timbre with such mechanical perfection.

23
00:01:29,428 --> 00:01:33,382
A human vocal cord has one resonant path.

24
00:01:33,402 --> 00:01:38,449
But an apex vocal mimic possesses two
separate acoustic

25
00:01:38,469 --> 00:01:43,782
voice boxes, splitting like the syrinx of
a lyrebird.

26
00:01:43,802 --> 00:01:47,915
A lyrebird can reproduce the metallic bite
of

27
00:01:47,935 --> 00:01:52,073
a chainsaw or the shrill cry of an infant.

28
00:01:52,093 --> 00:01:56,718
By vibrating both chambers at once, the
mimic crafts

29
00:01:56,738 --> 00:02:01,204
your sister's exact pitch and cadence in
the dark.

30
00:02:01,804 --> 00:02:04,833
Yet copying a voice is not speaking.

31
00:02:04,853 --> 00:02:12,121
The creature possesses no understanding of
human words, no memories, and no soul.

32
00:02:12,141 --> 00:02:15,448
It does not comprehend what it is saying.

33
00:02:15,468 --> 00:02:19,651
Like an ancient phonograph or a caged
parrot, it

34
00:02:19,671 --> 00:02:23,978
only knows how to replay recorded sound
waves.

35
00:02:23,998 --> 00:02:28,171
That is why it always repeats the
identical sentence

36
00:02:28,191 --> 00:02:31,846
twice, with the exact same breath pause.

37
00:02:31,866 --> 00:02:36,774
Outside my fence, the voice came again,
pitch-perfect

38
00:02:36,794 --> 00:02:40,700
and cold: Noah, please unlock the door.

39
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:42,792
Noah, please unlock the door.

40
00:02:43,392 --> 00:02:47,673
Up close, any person would see the
nightmare instantly.

41
00:02:47,693 --> 00:02:51,832
Its skin is pale as bleached bone,
stretched

42
00:02:51,852 --> 00:02:55,630
paper-thin over an elongated ribcage.

43
00:02:55,650 --> 00:02:58,063
So it never approaches the porch.

44
00:02:58,083 --> 00:03:02,782
It remains twenty-five paces back against
the dark pines.

45
00:03:02,802 --> 00:03:08,863
At night, cold ground air traps warm
layers above, bending sound waves

46
00:03:08,883 --> 00:03:15,134
back down across the soil so its whisper
carries hundreds of yards.

47
00:03:15,154 --> 00:03:18,324
It cannot see well in the pitch dark
either.

48
00:03:18,344 --> 00:03:25,058
Behind its hollow sockets sits a
reflective mirror layer, just like a deer.

49
00:03:25,078 --> 00:03:30,463
Those two glowing white dots beyond the
fence were not fireflies.

50
00:03:30,483 --> 00:03:31,561
They were its eyes.

51
00:03:32,161 --> 00:03:37,771
A predator with a frame that brittle
cannot survive a direct brawl.

52
00:03:37,791 --> 00:03:43,983
Its long, jointed limbs are built for
reaching and dragging, not wrestling.

53
00:03:44,003 --> 00:03:45,983
It cannot chase you down.

54
00:03:46,003 --> 00:03:49,984
Like an anglerfish lurking in the ocean
abyss, it

55
00:03:50,004 --> 00:03:54,040
depends entirely on a glowing lure to
survive.

56
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:58,090
And its lure is the one thing no human
heart

57
00:03:58,110 --> 00:04:02,405
can ignore: the voice of someone you love.

58
00:04:02,425 --> 00:04:06,630
It waits in the pitch black for you to
feel pity, step

59
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:10,796
past the threshold, and walk into its
reaching grasp.

60
00:04:11,396 --> 00:04:16,449
Standing in the dark of my cabin with my
palm sweating against

61
00:04:16,469 --> 00:04:21,412
the deadbolt, I remembered the creature's
one fatal flaw.

62
00:04:21,432 --> 00:04:27,682
It can mimic any syllable, but it can
never answer an unscripted question.

63
00:04:27,702 --> 00:04:33,067
I leaned against the heavy wood of the
door and called out into

64
00:04:33,087 --> 00:04:38,475
the yard: Mira, what did grandpa carve on
the cabin bench?

65
00:04:38,495 --> 00:04:42,975
A heavy, suffocating silence settled over
the pines.

66
00:04:42,995 --> 00:04:45,116
The night wind died down.

67
00:04:45,136 --> 00:04:49,837
For thirty seconds, not a twig snapped in
the forest.

68
00:04:49,857 --> 00:04:55,192
Then, from the black trees past the fence,
the voice replayed

69
00:04:55,212 --> 00:05:00,847
once more with identical pitch: Noah,
please unlock the door.

70
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:03,368
Noah, please unlock the door.

71
00:05:03,388 --> 00:05:08,041
I threw the secondary deadbolt and backed
away from the glass.

72
00:05:08,061 --> 00:05:11,383
And as I stepped into the shadows, a
nine-foot

73
00:05:11,403 --> 00:05:14,304
silhouette stepped onto the porch.

74
00:05:14,324 --> 00:05:22,016
This story was inspired by modern folklore
and the vocal anatomy of the forest mimic.

75
00:05:22,036 --> 00:05:23,245
Now tell me.

76
00:05:23,265 --> 00:05:24,806
Would you have opened the door?

